.TH BREW-WATCHTOWER 1 "2026-08-12" "brew-watchtower 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brew-watchtower \- manage grouped, scheduled Homebrew updates on macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brew-watchtower
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brew-watchtower
organizes Homebrew formulae and casks into named update groups.
Each item has an
.B auto
or
.B interactive
mode.
.PP
Automatic items may be upgraded by a background launchd job.
Interactive items are detected and reported by background jobs but are upgraded
only when
.B brew-watchtower run
is invoked from an attached terminal.
.PP
Checks and upgrades always run as the current Homebrew user and refuse to run
as root. Changes to group membership require administrator authorization because
the group registry is root-owned.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B groups
List all configured groups and the number of items in each group.
.TP
.B groups " [" init "|" sync "|" path "]"
List installed groups when called without an argument.
.B groups init
creates a user-owned declarative groups.conf template.
.B groups sync
validates and applies declared groups through the protected runtime, leaving
undeclared installed groups unchanged.
.B groups path
prints the manifest path.
.TP
.B list " [" GROUP "]"
List every configured item. If
.I GROUP
is supplied, list only that group's contents.
.TP
.BI "add " "GROUP TYPE TOKEN " [ MODE ]
Add an item to a group or replace the existing entry for the same token.
.I TYPE
must be
.B formula
or
.BR cask .
.I MODE
must be
.B auto
or
.BR interactive ,
and defaults to
.BR auto .
.IP
This command invokes sudo to update the root-owned group registry.
.TP
.BI "remove " "GROUP TOKEN"
Remove an item from a group. This command invokes sudo to update the root-owned
group registry.
.TP
.BI "check " GROUP
Refresh Homebrew metadata and report outdated members of
.IR GROUP .
No package upgrades are performed.
.TP
.BI "run " GROUP
Refresh Homebrew metadata, detect outdated members, and upgrade all
.B auto
members of
.IR GROUP .
.IP
When invoked from an attached terminal, outdated
.B interactive
members are also offered to Homebrew for upgrade. Under launchd, interactive
members are left pending and a macOS notification is generated.
.TP
.B status " [" GROUP "]"
Display the last recorded result and pending interactive items. If
.I GROUP
is omitted, display status for every group that has run.
.TP
.B drift
Check the entire configured Brewfile with
.BR "brew bundle check" .
The result is recorded for
.B blurb
without running
.B "brew update"
or processing any Watchtower group. This command exits non-zero when drift is
found.
.TP
.BI "drift fix " [ --clobber ]
Replace the configured Brewfile with a current
.BR "brew bundle dump" .
By default, the existing Brewfile is first saved beside it as
.IR Brewfile.backup-YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS .
.B --clobber
skips that backup.
.TP
.BI "drift restore " BACKUP
Restore a sibling backup created by
.BR "drift fix" .
The current Brewfile is first saved as a new timestamped backup.
.I BACKUP
must be the backup filename, not a path.
.PP
Set
.B auto_fix_brewfile_drift=1
in the user configuration to apply the same backup-first repair after a
Watchtower check or run detects drift. This is disabled by default; it does not
hook arbitrary Homebrew installs or upgrades. Use
.B brewfile_backup_keep
and
.B brewfile_backup_max_age_days
to prune Watchtower-created backups by count or age.
.TP
.B blurb
Print a compact shell-start status line when configured state is actionable.
This command reads only the user-owned Watchtower configuration and status
files; it never invokes Homebrew, Git, or the network.
.TP
.B config init
Create the default user-owned configuration file at
.I ~/.config/brew-watchtower/config .
.TP
.B config show
Print the effective user-owned presentation and Brewfile settings.
.TP
.B config path
Print the exact path of the user-owned configuration file.
.TP
.B setup [HOUR [MINUTE]]
Install or refresh the protected root-owned runtime, create the security group
if it does not exist, and install its user LaunchAgent. The default daily
schedule is 09:30. This command requests administrator authorization.
.TP
.BI "schedule " "GROUP HOUR MINUTE"
Create or replace the daily user LaunchAgent for
.IR GROUP .
The hour must be 0 through 23 and the minute 0 through 59. This command requests
administrator authorization.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed brew-watchtower version.
.TP
.BR help , " " -h , " " --help
Display a concise command summary.
.SH ITEM MODES
.TP
.B auto
The item may be upgraded without user interaction during a scheduled run.
Use this for software whose installation is reliably non-interactive and whose
temporary restart or termination is acceptable during the scheduled window.
.TP
.B interactive
Background runs detect and report the update but do not install it. A run from
an attached terminal attempts the upgrade, allowing Homebrew, macOS Installer,
or system-extension management to request authorization.
.PP
Changing an existing token's mode is done by adding it again:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower add security cask tailscale-app auto
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
List configured groups:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower groups
.fi
.PP
List the security group:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower list security
.fi
.PP
Add Firefox for unattended security updates:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower add security cask firefox auto
.fi
.PP
Add Tailscale as an interactive update:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower add security cask tailscale-app interactive
.fi
.PP
Add Git to a development-tools group:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower add dev-tools formula git auto
.fi
.PP
Check without installing anything:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower check security
.fi
.PP
Run the security group from a terminal:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower run security
.fi
.PP
Remove an item:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower remove security firefox
.fi
.SH SCHEDULING
brew-watchtower does not remain resident. User-level launchd jobs invoke it at
calendar intervals.
.PP
The initial security LaunchAgent runs:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower run security
.fi
.PP
daily at 09:30 local time. Because the job has no attached terminal,
interactive items are reported rather than installed.
.PP
The current launchd definition can be inspected with:
.PP
.nf
launchctl print "gui/$(id -u)/local.homebrew-autoupdate.security"
.fi
.PP
Create another daily schedule with:
.PP
.nf
brew-watchtower schedule dev-tools 5 0
.fi
.SH GROUP FILE FORMAT
Group files are tab-delimited declarative data with three fields:
.PP
.nf
TYPE    TOKEN    MODE
.fi
.PP
For example:
.PP
.nf
cask    tailscale-app    interactive
formula openssl@3        auto
.fi
.PP
Blank lines and lines beginning with a number sign are ignored. Group files are
never sourced or evaluated as shell code. Group names and all fields are
validated before use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/brew-watchtower/config
User-owned shell blurb, Brewfile drift, and generated-export settings.
.TP
.B ~/.config/brew-watchtower/Brewfile.generated
Optional generated snapshot of the installed Homebrew bundle. This never
replaces the curated Brewfile.
.TP
.B /Library/Application Support/Homebrew AutoUpdate/bin/autoupdate
Root-owned implementation used by both the command-line symlink and launchd.
.TP
.B /Library/Application Support/Homebrew AutoUpdate/groups/*.conf
Root-owned group registry.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/brew-watchtower
Command-line symlink used by a local installation. A Homebrew package instead
links the command from its Cellar into the Homebrew prefix.
.TP
.B ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.homebrew-autoupdate.*.plist
User-level launchd schedules.
.TP
.B ~/Library/Logs/Homebrew AutoUpdate/*.log
Per-group and launchd logs.
.TP
.B ~/Library/Application Support/Homebrew AutoUpdate/*.status
Last-run state and pending interactive items.
.TP
.B ~/Library/Caches/Homebrew AutoUpdate/update.lock
Global lock directory used to prevent overlapping runs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
brew-watchtower uses a fixed executable path of
.B /opt/homebrew/bin/brew
and supplies a minimal PATH.
.PP
Automated runs set Homebrew options that disable analytics, suppress environment
hints, disable automatic cleanup, and request non-interactive behavior.
Interactive entries run without Homebrew's non-interactive setting when invoked
from a terminal.
.SH SECURITY
brew-watchtower never runs Homebrew as root and never stores an administrator
password. The executable and group registry are owned by root. Runtime state,
logs, caches, and LaunchAgents belong to the user.
.PP
Root ownership prevents ordinary user-level software from silently changing the
persistent update policy. It does not prevent software already running as the
user from invoking Homebrew directly or creating another user LaunchAgent.
.PP
Homebrew casks and packages may execute vendor installers or package scripts.
Automatic mode should therefore be assigned only to trusted packages whose
installation behavior is suitable for unattended execution.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
Invalid input, an unknown group, a concurrent run, a Homebrew refresh failure,
or one or more failed upgrades.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1),
.BR launchctl (1),
.BR launchd.plist (5),
.BR sudo (8)
